{"sentences": [{"sentence_id": "s1", "sentence": "Ninety-nine trials test CD20-targeting drugs in multiple sclerosis (MS), with 47 in Phase 3 and 23 in Phase 4.", "cites": ["NCT06677710"]}, {"sentence_id": "s2", "sentence": "Roche leads with 35 trials, followed by Novartis with 16 and TG Therapeutics with 9.", "cites": ["NCT06677710"]}, {"sentence_id": "s3", "sentence": "Three CD20-targeting drugs—ocrelizumab, ofatumumab, and ublituximab—are approved for relapsing forms of MS.", "cites": ["NCT06677710"]}, {"sentence_id": "s4", "sentence": "Multiple trials have stopped: one due to business reasons, one due to slow enrollment, one due to funding loss, and another due to geopolitical conflict.", "cites": ["NCT06677710", "NCT05208840", "NCT04877457", "NCT04878211"]}, {"sentence_id": "s6", "sentence": "A 2026 pharmacovigilance study found signals of non-PML neuroinvasive infections with anti-CD20 therapies in MS.", "cites": ["PMID:42947820"]}, {"sentence_id": "s7", "sentence": "A 2026 perspective highlights uncertainty around anti-CD20 discontinuation, noting disease reactivation after cessation and lack of predictive biomarkers.", "cites": ["PMID:42991313"]}, {"sentence_id": "s8", "sentence": "A 2026 cohort study in JAMA Neurology reported an increased risk of inflammatory bowel disease following anti-CD20 treatment in MS.", "cites": ["PMID:42911175"]}, {"sentence_id": "s9", "sentence": "The median stop-risk for CD20 trials in MS is 0.249, based on the site's risk model.", "cites": ["RISK:cd20:MS"]}, {"sentence_id": "s10", "sentence": "FDA labels for ocrelizumab and ofatumumab include warnings for infections, infusion/injection reactions, immunoglobulin reduction, and malignancy risk.", "cites": ["FDA:9da42362-3bb5-4b83-b4bb-b59fd4e55f0d", "FDA:6a8a3f53-2062-48ff-9dbe-b939df133ca3"]}], "sources": [{"id": "NCT06677710", "text": "{"nct":"NCT06677710","title":"IDP-023 g-NK Cells Plus Ocrelizumab in Patients With Progressive Multiple Sclerosis","state":"stopped","drug":"ocr